/-
Root module of the default library `GW`. Scope and evidence: `README.md`; canonical and
archived modules, layer by layer: `docs/CODEMAP.md`.

Canonical layers:
* `GW.Endpoint.Kernel.*`, `GW.Endpoint.Coulomb.*`, `GW.Endpoint.{CertInterval,
  CertInverse, CertSexcut, NearPole, QPUnique}`: the Lean specification of the pinned
  BerkeleyGW 4.0 Si-EPM GPP calculation (`EpsSpec`, `SigmaSpec`, `RootSpec`;
  `docs/ENDPOINT.md` section 4) and the checkers behind its kernel-checked numerical
  certificates. The certificates (`GW/Endpoint/Kernel/Data`, generated) and the
  headline compositions without Coulomb-box hypothesis (`GW.Endpoint.Kernel.Headline`) are built only
  by the non-default target `GWKernelData`, so they are not imported here. The export of
  the run data and the correspondence between the Fortran and the specification are
  trusted, not proved.
* `GW.Endpoint.ManyBody.*`, `GW.Endpoint.HubbardDimer*`: kernel-checked theorems about
  the GW error structure of finite fermion models. They are not bounds for silicon.
* `GW.Bridge.*`: conditional theory-to-specification identities (`docs/BRIDGE.md`). The
  spec Σ and ε equal a theory-side Σ and static RPA ε plus named correction terms, under
  named hypotheses that are not instantiated on the certified run. Derived: the
  frequency/time structure, the HL-GPP kernel algebra and the static χ0/RPA structure.
  Shared with the spec by definition: the exchange, the plane-wave matrix elements and
  normalisation, the ε Coulomb, the common-system pair density (EpsSpec's `M`) and the HL
  Ω² helpers; `G0` is the T = 0 closed form, taken as a definition.
  * `FreqIntegral`, `GPPModel`, `Bloch`, `Compare` (BRIDGE); `EpsChi0`, `EpsBloch`,
    `EpsRPA`, `EpsCompare` (BRIDGE-EPS); `EpsQ0`, `EpsQ0Sigma` (BRIDGE-Q0); `Disc`
    (BRIDGE-DISC).
  * `Common` (R28-F1): the composition restated for screening and Σ data that are images
    of one data record `MF` with the Σ states on its grid (`sigA_compat`). `MF.TR`
    cannot hold for a block whose `neg` fixes a grid point with a nonzero sphere vector
    (`compat_selfpaired_no_TR`). For O1's X/L states the hypotheses of `sigA_compat` are
    unsatisfiable when every plan's `neg` encodes `-k` on a grid that stores each k-point class once, which fixes X and L
    (a trusted plan premise, not a theorem: `MF` has no k-coordinates), whose spheres hold a
    nonzero vector (`hyps_unsat_of_selfpaired`), or, for arbitrary plans, given `hnp` (no index holds the
    negated sphere list of X or L), checked numerically on the Si-EPM Σ grid
    (`hyps_unsat_of_unpaired`). Storing X/L once does not give `hnp`: a finite sphere does
    not determine k.
  * `Cor` (BRIDGE-COR): an enclosure of the omitted-band Coulomb-hole tail for an
    abstract `CompleteK κ` completion; the all-band `SigAall` keeps a static remainder
    `CORall`. `CorPerturb`, `CorPerturbLowdin` (R28-F3): the enclosure for every exact
    completion of orthonormal rows near the stored ones; not shown for the EPM's own
    eigenvectors (their distance is not evaluated). `CorResidual` (R28-F4): the exact
    split of `CORall` and sufficient conditions for it to vanish.
* Older lineages imported by `GW.Bridge`, hence canonical: `GW.GPP.PoleCancellation`;
  `GW.LL.Diagram`, `Ring`, `StructuralRing`, `Screening`, `Electronic`.

Archived (kept and frozen; superseded as recorded in `docs/CODEMAP.md`):
* the scalar pole-cancellation demo of `Specification.md` v0.1: `GW.GPP.FiniteSelfEnergy`,
  `GW.Examples`, `GW.GPP.BerkeleyGWMap`, `GW.GPP.PoleDomain`;
* `GW.BGW.M1Screening`, `M2Screening`, `M3Chi`, `M3Transfer`, `M4GPP`, `M5Sigma`: the
  single-block and single-mode certificates of earlier milestones;
* `GW.LL.RingHalfEdge`, `GW.LL.Wick`: the parked Lin-Lindsey classical Gibbs track.

`GW.Audit` is deliberately not imported here: it only runs `#print axioms` and
is checked separately with `lake env lean GW/Audit.lean`.

The import block below is GENERATED by `python3 scripts/registry.py`: every module of
the default library, sorted. `GWKernelData` modules are excluded. Do not edit it by
hand. Canonical vs archived modules: `docs/CODEMAP.md`.
-/
